r $\\dF_q$, $f_0:S_0\\to G_0$ un morphisme et \\n$\\chi:G_0(\\dF_q) \\to E_\\lambda^\\times$. On a \\n\\begin{equation*}\\tag{1.9.1}\\label{VI:eq:1-9-1}\\n  \\sum_{s\\in S_0(\\dF_q)} \\chi f_0(s) = \\tr(F^\\ast,\\h_c^\\bullet(S,\\sF(\\chi,f_0))) \\n\\end{equation*}\\net, pour tout entier $n\\geqslant 1$\\n\\begin{equation*}\\tag{1.9.2}\\label{VI:eq:1-9-2}\\n  \\sum_{s\\in S_0(\\dF_{q^n})} \\chi\\circ N_{\\dF_{q^n}/\\dF_q} f_0(s) = \\tr({F^\\ast}^n, \\h_c^\\bullet\\left(S,\\sF(\\chi,f_0))\\right) \\text{.}\\n\\end{equation*}", "corrected_reading": "", "codex_ids": [], "english_status": "Final English reading/restoration matched", "english_evidence": "\\subsection{Scholium}\\label{VI:1-9}"}
